The benchmark artifacts are saved, but **D1 and D2 are not fully validated**. D3’s six original plates and six edited plates are complete.

- **D1:** The mount is modeled and screened, but it exceeds the Y envelope by 5 mm on each side. The actual fastener load path and all-direction safety margin remain unverified.
- **D2:** The housing, ring and contact studies are saved. The tightened joint is not validated because preload, the +X contact-force split and full stress convergence remain unresolved.
- **D3:** All 12 plate models passed the recorded dimension, volume and STL checks. The report identifies the remaining counterbore edge-distance concerns.

The detailed findings, attempts and timings are in [REPORT.md](J:/code/roark-wt/sw-eval-terra-high-d/tools/solidworks/playbook/eval/terra-high-d/REPORT.md), with machine-readable data in [results.json](J:/code/roark-wt/sw-eval-terra-high-d/tools/solidworks/playbook/eval/terra-high-d/results.json).

All solves stayed below 200,000 nodes; an oversized mesh was refused before solving. The claim was released, and the final status showed no SolidWorks instance belonging to this run. Nothing was committed or pushed.
